{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/558841-chernobog-is-here","id":558841,"title":"Chernobog is here!!!!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-17T16:52:51-07:00","id":558841,"title":"Chernobog is here!!!!","content":"I've been STing a Changeling the Lost Campaign for about 2 years now and we are coming up to the resolution of the overall story arch. To make a long story short, the players have been dealing with the Sun and Moon courts in Miami. They have discovered the reason why both courts have ventured out of their Slavic homeland. The Moon court is in some dark shit and the sun court is trying to uphold the law and bring them back for judgement. <br /> What has the moon court done to deserve this Wyld hunt? They have actually made a pack with not just a true Fae but the Dark God Chernobog. As far as I understand, Demons grow the more popular they get. The more people know of them the more powerful they get.<br /> <br /> I have them seeking out The Lord Sages of the Unknown Reaches and I'm going to have them hook them up with a pack of Storm Lords. I need help creating Chernobog. He's damn near god like so I just need a really good Bane and Ban.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have any suggestions?<br /> <br /> Please and thank you all!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The land doesn't forget. I'm not prone to, either.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5367-inphobia812","name":"Inphobia812","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5367_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T18:27:09-07:00","id":558922,"title":"","content":"Considering that Disney is a much a valid source as anything for the apocryphal &quot;Black God&quot;, and certainly a evocative well, maybe something like he must flee from the light of the sun, or that he has the sound of church bells as a Bane?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T12:14:16-07:00","id":559662,"title":"","content":"The earliest available sources describe Chernobog as more-or-less a personification of evil, the source of all misfortune. He doesn't seem to have had much of a personality of his own, and may, in fact, have been a relatively late mythological figure inspired by the Christian Devil. His ban could be something along the lines of him being unable to do anything that he knows would benefit another, rendering him capable only of causing purposeless suffering.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it's conceivable that Chernobog (which after all simply means &quot;Black God&quot;) was an epithet or kenning for some other deity. The strongest candidate would seem to be Veles, who was part of a dualistic rivalry with the supreme thunder god Perun. Veles was said to be lord of the underworld, and was sometimes anthropomorphized but at other times depicted as a huge serpent or dragon.<br /> <br /> According to some scholars (particularly the philologists Vyacheslav Vsevolodovich Ivanov and Vladimir Toporov), Veles was, among other things, a trickster who was always trying to steal something from Perun (usually his cattle). Thunder and lightning were said to be caused by the two battling in the sky, and the ensuing rain (which poured forth from Veles' battered body) marked the triumph of Perun. Veles never stayed dead for long, though, and soon enough would be up to his old tricks again.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to draw a connection to this myth, you could have Chernobog's bane be something related to thunderstorms; perhaps wood from a cross that was struck by lightning. Maybe his ban could be that he has to retreat underground when confronted with the sound of thunder or the sight of lightning. This might be particularly thematically appropriate for you, since you're planning to have a group of Storm Lords join the fight against him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 06-18-2015, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T12:55:01-07:00","id":559716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/558841-chernobog-is-here?p=559662#post559662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you wanted to draw a connection to this myth, you could have Chernobog's bane be something related to thunderstorms; perhaps wood from a cross that was struck by lightning. Maybe his ban could be that he has to retreat underground when confronted with the sound of thunder or the sight of lightning. This might be particularly thematically appropriate for you, since you're planning to have a group of Storm Lords join the fight against him.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a great suggestion! I second it!<br /> <br /> <br /> Possible bane: the spear of the Bogatyr Dobrynya Nikitich. This works with the Veles connection that CatDoom mentioned, since it's a dragon slaying weapon. Even if you don't connect Chernobog to Veles, it's still the spear of a mighty hero. You might add the requirement that it be dipped in the blood of a dragon (which could be interpereted loosely - maybe a Draconic Fairest would work or even a Vampire of the Ordo Dracul). The added bonus of this weapon is that you can drop clues and then have your players do actual research into real life folktales to find the answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T15:59:21-07:00","id":559923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/558841-chernobog-is-here?p=559662#post559662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you wanted to draw a connection to this myth, you could have Chernobog's bane be something related to thunderstorms; perhaps wood from a cross that was struck by lightning. Maybe his ban could be that he has to retreat underground when confronted with the sound of thunder or the sight of lightning. This might be particularly thematically appropriate for you, since you're planning to have a group of Storm Lords join the fight against him.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love this! Thank you!!!!!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The land doesn't forget. I'm not prone to, either.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5367-inphobia812","name":"Inphobia812","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5367_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T16:21:36-07:00","id":559954,"title":"","content":"There's also an interesting interpretation of Chernobog in American gods, where he is taken as less &quot;embodiment of evil&quot; and more &quot;inevitability of bad things happening&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T14:49:46-07:00","id":563424,"title":"","content":"This is just how to portray him, but I think this could be useful. One thing that applies to Chernobog, as well as all other our gods is '' there are as much evil gods as there are good ones.'' Chernobog looks evil, and is certainly such to humans, but he doesn't think about that. Morality and limits are something he simply cannot comprehend. He walks out in world, dreamy and dazed, lost in his own thoughts. It is cute somewhat-if it wasn't for fact that his giant body was pure shadow in black armor, with burning eyes, fangs and talons. As he walks, colours wash out of land. Plants and animals dies, land and sky mix, and night approaches. He draws blood, and causes suffering- not because he is sadistic, but because he believes it to be his holy duty. Maybe it is.<br /> But hate is just love from another direction. He is slow, and childlike, cooing over all his victims, petting and ripping them, letting them know there are none undeserving of being visited by him. He loves us all<br /> From opposite direction of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6005-coolcat12345","name":"coolcat12345","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T05:31:56-07:00","id":573793,"title":"","content":"Well, IIRC Rank 6+ Ephamera only work through Rank 5 Royal Avatars (a de-powered part of themselves). So give him stats appropriate for a Rank 5 entity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}